First Author: Tian
Title: Machine Learning–Based Prognostic Model for Patients After Lung Transplantation
Source number: 50  ￼

Very short summary: This retrospective prognostic study developed a random survival forest (RSF) model to predict overall survival after lung transplantation. Five key findings were: (1) 504 adult lung transplant recipients were included, split into 353 training and 151 test patients; (2) 16 variables were selected for the final RSF model from 22 candidate characteristics; (3) postoperative ECMO time was the most important predictor; (4) the RSF model achieved excellent test-set performance with iAUC 0.879 and iBS 0.130; and (5) the RSF model significantly outperformed the benchmark Cox model and stratified patients into prognostically distinct risk groups. Figures 1–3 and Tables 1–2 were directly used for this extraction.  ￼

