	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The paper developed an “RSF model” for overall survival and used a Cox regression model as the benchmark comparator. Patients were randomly assigned to training and test sets at a 7:3 ratio. Feature selection used RSF variable importance with bootstrapping, and “grid search” was used for hyperparameter tuning. No SHAP/LIME-type interpretability was reported.  ￼

Section 4: AI Quality & Reproducibility (CONVINCE Standards)
