	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The methods state that missing data were handled “by multiple imputation by chained equations.” The training and test sets included 353 and 151 patients, respectively. Data preprocessing included random split, feature selection by bootstrapped variable importance, and hold-out validation. Class imbalance is not especially applicable for time-to-event survival modeling. No code-release statement was identified.  ￼

