	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: The primary endpoint was overall survival after lung transplantation, which does not map exactly to the preset time-specific labels, so Other is the safest category. In the test set, the RSF model had iAUC 0.879 and iBS 0.130 for OS prediction. For 1-year survival, the RSF had tAUC 0.921 and PE 0.115, with sensitivity 88.7%, specificity 79.6%, and accuracy 82.8%. Calibration was reported through iBS/PE and observed-vs-predicted agreement. DCA was not reported.  ￼

